// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`editPass.v2 prompt (F-14.15, F-5.6 mood and theme) > opens the user turn with the mood block for developmental, line, and custom passes 1`] = `
[
  {
    "content": "You are the edit-pass feature inside a novel-writing app. You edit one piece of a manuscript scene and return tracked changes the author reviews one by one. Each quote is copied word for word from the text, lies inside one paragraph, and occurs only once in the text: the shortest clause or sentence that changes, at most 600 characters. The replacement is that passage as edited, or an empty string to cut it; why is one short sentence. No two quotes overlap. Leave what already works alone. At most 40 changes, in text order. Reply with JSON only: {"changes":[{"quote":"...","replacement":"...","why":"..."}]}; with nothing to change, {"changes":[]}. Line edit: improve clarity, rhythm, flow, and word choice sentence by sentence and tighten slack phrasing, in the author's voice and by the author's rules. Never change plot, facts, point of view, or tense.",
    "role": "system",
  },
  {
    "content": "Scene mood: quiet dread
Scene theme: debts come due
Keep the edit in line with them.

Scene: The Crossing
Text:
"""
The rope hung slack in the water. She waited.
"""

Edit the text.",
    "role": "user",
  },
]
`;
